WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.149 --> 00:00:03.100
So the grift in the corruption, you're both
coming full circle.

00:00:03.100 --> 00:00:10.179
Rudy Giuliani has reportedly discussed a blanket
preemptive pardon from President Donald Trump

00:00:10.179 --> 00:00:13.639
in these last seven weeks before Trump leaves
office.

00:00:13.639 --> 00:00:19.160
Trump also reportedly considering preemptive
blanket pardons for three of his children,

00:00:19.160 --> 00:00:23.009
as well as his son in law, Jared Kushner.

00:00:23.009 --> 00:00:28.001
The New York Times can report, based on multiple
sources told about the conversation, that

00:00:28.001 --> 00:00:32.900
Rudy Giuliani as recently as last week was
talking to Donald Trump about a pardon.

00:00:32.900 --> 00:00:38.560
It's not clear as of yet whether Rudy Giuliani
originally brought it up to Trump or whether

00:00:38.560 --> 00:00:40.780
Trump brought it up to Giuliani.

00:00:40.780 --> 00:00:43.460
But there have now reportedly been multiple
conversations.

00:00:43.460 --> 00:00:46.270
The most recent one was last week.

00:00:46.270 --> 00:00:52.340
Donald Trump has reportedly not yet decided
what he will do about pardoning Rudy Giuliani.

00:00:52.340 --> 00:00:57.190
And the same questions remain about Trump
pardoning Jared Kushner as well as his children,

00:00:57.190 --> 00:00:59.900
Ivanka Don Jr. and Eric.

00:00:59.900 --> 00:01:03.630
Now, Trump reportedly not considering a pardon
for Tiffany Trump.

00:01:03.630 --> 00:01:07.740
I guess he doesn't expect that she might be
charged with anything.

00:01:07.740 --> 00:01:09.730
But the immediate question is pardon?

00:01:09.730 --> 00:01:10.730
From what?

00:01:10.730 --> 00:01:12.780
Rudy hasn't even been charged with anything.

00:01:12.780 --> 00:01:13.960
Neither have his children.

00:01:13.960 --> 00:01:17.909
And that is exactly the question that's raising
the most attention.

00:01:17.909 --> 00:01:22.490
It's not actually clear what Rudy Giuliani
might be charged with in the future, but the

00:01:22.490 --> 00:01:27.780
fact that it's being discussed multiple times
at the highest levels is very interesting.

00:01:27.780 --> 00:01:32.659
We know that Rudy was being investigated last
summer by federal investigators for maybe

00:01:32.659 --> 00:01:36.470
violating lobbying law through the work he
did with Ukraine.

00:01:36.470 --> 00:01:38.420
But beyond that, it's not exactly clear.

00:01:38.420 --> 00:01:43.979
Now, what we do know is that as a general
concept, the idea here is that with regard

00:01:43.979 --> 00:01:48.450
to his children and son in law, at least,
and it may be similar with Rudy Giuliani,

00:01:48.450 --> 00:01:54.370
Donald Trump believes that there will be partizan
investigations and possibly prosecutions of

00:01:54.370 --> 00:01:57.700
his children after he leaves office.

00:01:57.700 --> 00:02:03.200
And so it's not because from Trump's perspective,
it's not that he thinks his kids committed

00:02:03.200 --> 00:02:04.220
crimes.

00:02:04.220 --> 00:02:05.869
It's that he thinks they didn't.

00:02:05.869 --> 00:02:08.050
But they might be charged with crimes anyway.

00:02:08.050 --> 00:02:09.739
Bipartisan partizan Joe Biden administration.

00:02:09.739 --> 00:02:10.739
What?

00:02:10.739 --> 00:02:13.790
You know, there's this funny thing.

00:02:13.790 --> 00:02:23.879
Trump always projects his immorality and his
do whatever for a buck or whatever for revenge

00:02:23.879 --> 00:02:26.730
sort of attitude on other people.

00:02:26.730 --> 00:02:32.430
Trump is worried Biden would go after Trump's
kids even though they didn't do anything as

00:02:32.430 --> 00:02:36.980
far as Trump is concerned, because that's
exactly what Trump would do if he were Joe

00:02:36.980 --> 00:02:37.980
Biden.

00:02:37.980 --> 00:02:42.540
But Joe Biden has clearly shown no interest
and has even said he has no plan to direct

00:02:42.540 --> 00:02:45.409
his Justice Department to do anything of the
sort.

00:02:45.409 --> 00:02:50.930
But a lot of Trump's behavior is motivated
by what Trump imagines he would do if in someone

00:02:50.930 --> 00:02:52.290
else's position.

00:02:52.290 --> 00:02:58.790
Now, Rudy Giuliani's spokeswoman was asked
about the seeking a pardon and she said Giuliani

00:02:58.790 --> 00:03:03.389
can't comment on any discussions he's had
with his client, Trump being his client.

00:03:03.389 --> 00:03:11.139
So what we're talking about here are blanket,
broad, open ended preemptive pardons.

00:03:11.139 --> 00:03:13.420
This is very rare, but it has happened in
the past.

00:03:13.420 --> 00:03:14.420
George Washington.

00:03:14.420 --> 00:03:16.559
Yeah, we have to go, but we don't have to
go back that far.

00:03:16.559 --> 00:03:21.760
But one notable example goes back to George
Washington who pardoned those who were plotting

00:03:21.760 --> 00:03:26.870
the Whiskey Rebellion so that they wouldn't
be prosecuted for treason.

00:03:26.870 --> 00:03:31.309
Gerald Ford pardoned Richard Nixon for all
his actions as president.

00:03:31.309 --> 00:03:35.639
Now, it is important to remember a few important
things about presidential pardons.

00:03:35.639 --> 00:03:39.230
Number one, they work for federal crimes,
not state crimes.

00:03:39.230 --> 00:03:43.689
So if the Southern District of New York, as
an example, were to bring charges against

00:03:43.689 --> 00:03:46.530
Rudy or Ivonka or whoever, we're still not
sure for what.

00:03:46.530 --> 00:03:50.230
But if they did, the pardon from Trump wouldn't
protect them there.

00:03:50.230 --> 00:03:56.109
Number two, whether preemptive blanket pardons
work is a legal question.

00:03:56.109 --> 00:03:59.639
And what I mean by that is a president can
do it.

00:03:59.639 --> 00:04:04.930
And in the past, these preemptive pardons
have dissuaded anybody from prosecuting the

00:04:04.930 --> 00:04:05.930
pardoned individuals.

00:04:05.930 --> 00:04:12.790
Like, for example, when Gerald Ford pardoned
Richard Nixon, the pardon was challenged legally.

00:04:12.790 --> 00:04:16.909
It was found to be constitutional, but it
was never brought to the Supreme Court.

00:04:16.909 --> 00:04:24.080
It is conceivable that a Supreme Court could
say a blanket preemptive pardon is not OK.

00:04:24.080 --> 00:04:26.720
Whether it ever gets to the Supreme Court
is a question.

00:04:26.720 --> 00:04:31.889
And, you know, with with the Supreme Court,
we have right now, I'm not sure this Supreme

00:04:31.889 --> 00:04:37.250
Court is going to rule against blanket preemptive
pardons from Donald Trump.

00:04:37.250 --> 00:04:38.660
So that's one part of this.

00:04:38.660 --> 00:04:43.270
Now, as far as Donald Trump is concerned,
he just pardoned his convicted former national

00:04:43.270 --> 00:04:45.930
security adviser, Michael Flynn, last week.

00:04:45.930 --> 00:04:50.020
He previously commuted the sentence of Roger
Stone.

00:04:50.020 --> 00:04:51.020
He also.

00:04:51.020 --> 00:04:56.389
And less well-known people now, just a funny
side note, things are so crazy right now that

00:04:56.389 --> 00:05:00.810
when I read the original headline about this
story, I thought maybe Rudy and Trump talked

00:05:00.810 --> 00:05:03.090
about Trump pardoning Trump.

00:05:03.090 --> 00:05:08.830
The first headline I saw said something like,
Giuliani discussed a preemptive pardon with

00:05:08.830 --> 00:05:09.830
Trump.

00:05:09.830 --> 00:05:13.139
That could mean Giuliani talked to Trump about
Trump pardoning Rudy.

00:05:13.139 --> 00:05:18.020
But it could also mean that as his lawyer,
Giuliani talked to Trump about Trump pardoning

00:05:18.020 --> 00:05:22.160
himself and a self pardon is a completely
different story.

00:05:22.160 --> 00:05:25.070
Unclear whether that is something Donald Trump
could do.

00:05:25.070 --> 00:05:30.051
So the long and short of it is Rudy wants
immunity for everything, no matter what, in

00:05:30.051 --> 00:05:32.870
perpetuity and a sort of free pass.

00:05:32.870 --> 00:05:34.879
And that would be four things.

00:05:34.879 --> 00:05:37.479
What let me see how I can say this the right
way.

00:05:37.479 --> 00:05:41.220
The the pardon can't be for things that you
do after the pardon.

00:05:41.220 --> 00:05:46.050
So in other words, if Rudy is pardoned and
the next day commits a federal crime, the

00:05:46.050 --> 00:05:50.439
legal consensus is that would not be covered
by a presidential pardon.

00:05:50.439 --> 00:05:52.020
We're going to follow it.

00:05:52.020 --> 00:06:54.770
Many pardons coming from Donald Trump in the
next seven weeks 

00:06:54.770 --> 00:07:06.860
for sure.

